ADDENDA <Act No. 18187, May 18, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to suspension of operation of aircraft of foreigners providing international air transport services)
The amended provisions of Article 105(1)5 shall begin to apply where a foreigner providing international air transport services requires a pilot to perform aviation services when he or she cannot normally do so under the influence of alcohol, etc., in violation of Article 57(1) which is applied mutatis mutandis pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 106(1), after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning designation of synthetic flight trainer)
(1) A flight simulator designated by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport pursuant to the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed designated for one year from the date on which this Act enters into force pursuant to the amended provisions of the main clause of Article 39-2(4).
(2) Flight control or flight experience with a flight simulator recognized pursuant to the previous provisions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed flight control or flight experience with a synthetic flight trainer under the amended provisions of subparagraph 15 of Article 2.

