ADDENDA <Act No. 18789, Jan. 18, 2022>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Article 41-2 and 166(1)1 shall enter into force one year after the date of the promulgation, and the amended provisions of Article 42(2) through (5), 43(1)8-2 and 8-3, 47-2(1)6 and 7, 135(6)1-2 shall enter into force three years after the date of the promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to restrictions on applying for examinations)
The amended provisions of Article 43(4) and 47-2(3) shall begin to apply to persons who are suspended from taking the relevant examination, review, or aviation medical examination or who receive the disposition of invalidation after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to application for designation of aviation medical examiners)
The amended provisions of Article 50(2) shall begin to apply to persons who receive the disposition to revoke the designation of an aviation medical examiner pursuant to Article 50(1) after this Act enters into force.

