ADDENDUM <Act No. 20051, Jan. 16, 2024>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force one year after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Article 129 shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation and those of each subparagraph of Article 135(5) and (8) and Article 136(1) shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparations for safety education on ultra-light vehicle)
Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems it necessary for the enforcement of this Act, he or she may designate an institution or organization that may entrust affairs concerning safety education related to ultra-light vehicles under the amended provisions of Article 135(9) before this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning safety certification of ultra-light vehicle)
A person who has obtained certification of ultra-light vehicle pilot who is required to undergo safety education under the amended provisions of Article 125-2(1) as at the time this Act enters into force shall undergo safety education under the same amended provisions within two years from the date this Act enters into force.

