ADDENDA <Act No. 20981, May 27, 2025>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Article 6-2 shall enter into force 3 months after the date of its promulgation, and the amended provisions of Article 42-2, Article 43 (applicable only to matters regarding air traffic control aptitude tests), Articles 44(4), 45(6), 134(9), and 136(1) (applicable only to matters regarding air traffic control aptitude tests) shall enter into force 3 years after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional measures concerning certification of qualification of certified air traffic controllers)
(1) A person prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport who has been granted certification of qualification of air traffic controller in accordance with the previous provisions at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have been granted certification of qualification of certified air traffic controller under the amended provisions of Article 35(7)-2 and a rating on certification of qualification of certified air traffic controller under the amended provisions of Article 37(1)3. In such cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may determine and notify the air traffic control facilities subject to the rating on certification of qualification of certified air traffic controller.
(2) The amended provisions of Article 34(2)1c shall not apply to a person under 21 years of age who is deemed to have been granted certification of qualification of certified air traffic controller under paragraph (1).

